# MANIFOLD Vision

> **Field computation. Not a game engine. A continuity engine.**

## The Core Insight

Traditional software is built on discrete components: entities, components, systems (ECS). Objects exist at points, move along paths, and interact through collisions.

Field computation is different. Everything is a **continuous tensor field**. A terrain isn't a mesh — it's a density field with cohesion and permeability channels. A character isn't an entity at (x,y,z) — it's a local maximum in the density field with a gradient defining its velocity. A building isn't a damaged/undamaged flag — it's a region of the material tensor with reduced cohesion.

## Why This Matters

| Domain | Discrete Approach | Field Approach |
|--------|------------------|----------------|
| Terrain | Heightmap + LOD | 6-channel tensor, erosion physics |
| Games | ECS + physics engine | Tensor ECS, gradient agents |
| Simulation | Grid + particle systems | Conservation-enforced field computation |
| AI | Behavior trees + navmesh | Gradient-following agents, field awareness |
| Number Theory | Sieve + search | Stride-24 corridor, vinculum constraints |

## The MANIFOLD Ecosystem

```
hyperpoly-terrain (GPU substrate)
    ↓
flux-chamber (runtime layer)
    ↓
aetherion-continuum (planet-scale)
    ↓
trench-builder (open world demo)
    ↓
guinea-pig-trench-portal (browser games)
    ↓
prompt-asset-writer (documentation vinculum)
    ↓
erdos-straus-solver (mathematical research)
```

Each layer is a vinculum — it preserves something (the field computation model) and sacrifices something (domain-specific optimizations). The ecosystem is the set of all vinculums that share the same algebraic skeleton.

## Vinculum Principles

1. **Every operation is a ratio**. A vinculum is a bar between two terms. The top is what you want, the bottom is what you have, the bar is the transformation.

2. **Every design is a tradeoff**. Every vinculum preserves something and sacrifices something. Document both.

3. **The substrate changes, the computation doesn't**. The same 6-channel tensor that simulates terrain also calibrates LiDAR arrays, coordinates drone swarms, and documents legal cases.

4. **Continuity is not a feature. It's the platform.**
